# The test that an array holds an element at a position has code for each storage kind, at an index, at any integer and at any number, as a value, as the condition of a branch and as the condition that a TestAndBranch owns, in the three code shapes.
# A position outside the length, a hole and a number that is no index fail it. So it calls nothing, where the test that `in` is compiled to looks a name up. It takes the position as it comes, as an integer or as a double.
# The storage kind is proven by the type of the array or by a guard, and nothing is asked of the prototypes: none of these arrays is pristine
# FORM: Placed
# OPTIONS: heat=OnlyLoopsAreHot check=validate-back-end
# RUN: generate-code calls
# RUN(S): code-shapes
# RUN(R): pass ChooseRepresentations

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js"
function f0 name="valueInInt32AtNumber" parameters=[{type=Array<i32, proven, Int32>}, {type=number}] results=[{type=boolean}] {
    v2 = IsElementPresent v0, v1 arrayStorage=Int32
    Return v2
}
# CHECK: f0: size={{*}} frame=none
# R-LABEL: function f0 name="valueInInt32AtNumber"
# R: v1: number @Double):
# R-NEXT: v2: boolean @Boolean = IsElementPresent v0, v1 arrayStorage=Int32
function f1 name="valueInDoubleAtNumber" parameters=[{type=Array<number, proven, Double>}, {type=number}] results=[{type=boolean}] {
    v2 = IsElementPresent v0, v1 arrayStorage=Double
    Return v2
}
